  "an3.59:1.2": "“Sacrifice” is _yañña_, a ritual slaughter of an animal such as a goat or sheep. | An “offering of food for ancestors” is _saddha_ (Sanskrit _śraddha_). | A “dish of milk-rice prepared for an auspicious ceremony” is _thālipāka_, literally “cooked in pot”. It was used for household offerings for fertility, etc. (Bṛhadāraṇyaka Upaniṣad 6.4.19). ",
